  "schema": 1,
  "seed": "For every selection and starting source state independently empty Cargos on A and on B. One agreed baseline cold target+shared is copied independently with type/bytes/names/mode/mtime/hardlink checks into A/B training roots. Settle each image on that state only; identify migration separately. Before each scored A or B trial mount a completely new empty root/product/shared COW upper over its respective trained, single-state, immutable lower; fail if a previous trial is reused. Never consume the first transition used by another trial. Pin exact starting and ending root hashes and native store identities. Host exclusively assigned; floor both ext4 24GiB and tmpfs 16GiB, always before and after each arm. Stop if reserve fails. Conservative upper allocation check before score.",
  "source_inventory": "261b3e5e70dd474df1b99c8d879ee37554eefa2058775632ee6059804e7df380",
  "statistics": "Primary per eligible command is the sum of real edit plus first unchanged durations. Report actual arm clock medians, paired median signed milliseconds and 100*(A-B)/A percentage. Two-sided exact paired sign tests and Holm across the 3 registered primary commands; assign unqualified commands p=1. 20,000 resamples stratified by historical direction and arm order for median percentages and milliseconds, linear 2.5/97.5% quantiles. Per-direction estimates AND intervals for total, edit, repeat (stratify within direction by arm order). Report unconditional and order/tail adverse observations. For a wall speed claim require primary lower interval above zero and adjusted p<.05, plus separate standalone first-unchanged noninferiority upper bound on candidate cost at most 3% AND at most 5 ms (lower savings >=-3%, >=-5ms); inability to establish that bound is not proof of a slowdown. Other phases and contrasts descriptive. Never combine rejected command rows or substitute another selector.",
